@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+---
+name: presentation
+description: Creates or modifies a browser presentation built as one evolving diagrammatic scene (stable entities moving through named steps) from a topic. Scaffolds the Vite + React + TypeScript app and scene kit when missing, then builds, renders, and visually checks the result. Use when asked to make, create, update, or modify a presentation, talk, or slide-like explainer.
+---
+
+# Presentation
+
+A presentation is **one scene** that evolves through ordered, named steps. Entities keep a stable
+identity and morph in place between steps; they are not independent slides. "Talk" is only an
+informal synonym (the per-presentation entry file is `Talk.tsx`).
+
+Everything below is relative to this file's directory (`SKILL_DIR`, the folder holding this
+`SKILL.md`). Resolve `templates/` and `scripts/` from there, never from the user's current
+working directory.
+
+## 0. Decide: create or modify
+
+- **Create** a new presentation → steps 1 to 5.
+- **Modify** an existing one → step 3 (target) and the scoped path in step 4. If the request does not
+  clearly name a presentation, list the registered presentations (slug and title from
+  `src/presentations/index.ts`) and ask which one before changing anything. Then ask only about the
+  requested changes (steps, entities, or style). Do not re-walk the full create interview.
+
+## 1. Gather requirements (create)
+
+Ask **one question at a time**. Cover, in this order, only what the prompt does not already give:
+
+1. the topic,
+2. the visual style (palette, typography, mood),
+3. the content and visual description of each step (title, caption, what appears, moves, connects).
+
+Never assume details the user can still provide. The user decides how much to specify: if they say to
+build with partial detail, do so from what you captured, with no completeness gate, and offer to
+iterate afterwards. If the prompt already holds the topic, style and every step, skip the questions.
+For a key or complex step you may draw an ASCII mockup and confirm the layout; do not do this for
+every step.
+
+## 2. Resolve the target and scaffold what is missing
+
+```bash
+node SKILL_DIR/scripts/presentation-scaffold.mjs detect <project-dir>
+```
+
+The JSON names the `target` app directory, which `anchors` exist, and what is `missing`. The three
+contract anchors are:
+
+1. **Build setup**: a Vite + React + TypeScript app with a working `npm run build`.
+2. **Scene kit**: `src/presentation-kit/` (the `Step`/`Scene` contract, stage, navigation, chrome).
+3. **Presentation index**: `src/presentations/index.ts`, the registry mapping each slug to a route.
+
+Detection is by contract, so cosmetic differences do not trigger re-scaffolding.
+
+Target rules: an empty or standalone project is scaffolded at its root; inside a monorepo
+(`workspaces`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, or a `packages/`/`apps/` layout) the app is scaffolded as its own
+self-contained app in `presentations/`; a project that already has the kit or the index is used as is.
+
+If `needsConfirmation` is true (the project is non-empty and lacks the kit or the index), tell the user
+the exact target directory and what will be written, and **proceed only after they confirm**.
+
+```bash
+node SKILL_DIR/scripts/presentation-scaffold.mjs scaffold <project-dir> [--yes]
+```
+
+This writes only the missing anchors, never overwrites existing files, adds any missing dependencies to
+`package.json`, and runs the install. Do not assume any dependency is already installed (React, Vite,
+TypeScript, Motion, Lucide, ESLint, Playwright). The scaffold also installs the Chromium build that
+`npm run verify` and `npm run inspect` launch (`npx playwright install chromium`; run it yourself if
+either reports that Chromium could not be launched). If the project already has an entry file
+(`src/main.tsx`), the scaffold moves it to `src/app-main.tsx` and puts a routed entry in its place, so
+presentation routes render while every other path still shows the host app. The scaffold is styling-framework neutral and ships no
+colors, fonts, spacing, card or button styles. If every anchor exists, skip scaffolding entirely.
+
+## 3. Generate or modify
+
+Create (from `<target>`):
+
+```bash
+node SKILL_DIR/scripts/presentation-scaffold.mjs add <target> --slug <slug> --title "<Title>"
+```
+
+This copies `templates/presentation/` to `src/presentations/<slug>/` and adds one line to the registry.
+Existing presentations stay untouched. Then replace the starter content:
+
+- `entities.ts`: the presentation's own `layoutId` namespace. One id per entity for the whole talk.
+- `steps/*.ts`: one `Step` per beat: stable `id`, `era` (section label), `title` (one line),
+  `caption` (paragraph), and a `payload` listing every entity visible at that step. Give adjacent
+  steps of the same diagram the same `groupKey` so the scene persists and entities morph instead of
+  remounting. Keep earlier entity ids in later steps; omit an id to make it animate out.
+- `Scene.tsx`: composes kit primitives (`Box`, `Label`, `Arrow`, `Frame`, `Emphasis`, `SymbolChip`,
+  `SceneLayer`). Use `appear` only for newcomers. Use raw coordinates on the 880 × 380 design canvas;
+  fit scaling is automatic.
+- `style.css`: **the presentation owns its look.** Plain CSS is the default, unless the host already uses
+  a styling framework or the user asked for one. Never add colors, fonts, borders, shadows or theme
+  tokens to `src/presentation-kit/`. Style the stable hooks: `[data-presentation-active]` (active
+  progress and table-of-contents entries), `[data-presentation-attribution]`, `[data-presentation-kind]`,
+  and the entity class names you set.
+
+Mark a subtree whose overlap is intentional and readable with `allowOverlap` (renders
+`data-presentation-allow-overlap`). Mark nothing else.
+
+Modify: make scoped edits to the identified presentation only (and its registry line if the slug or
+title changes).
+
+## 4. Self-verify before reporting done
+
+Run, from `<target>`, and fix everything that fails; never report success on broken output:
+
+```bash
+npm run build                                   # no type errors
+npm run verify                                  # build plus render of every registered presentation
+npm run inspect -- <slug>                       # settled per-step screenshots + advisory warnings
+```
+
+`npm run verify` renders every step in Chromium on `127.0.0.1` and fails on any console error, uncaught
+error, or step that does not advance. While iterating you may run a lighter build plus a first-step
+render, but the first-step render must show no runtime or console error before you finish.
+
+Visual composition check: look at the screenshots under `inspection/<slug>/` (or an equivalent browser
+view) for the **first step, the last step, and every dense or key step**. For presentations that are
+sensitive to width, also capture a narrow viewport (`--viewport 480x800`). Important content must fit
+the canvas, intentional overlaps must stay readable, and nothing may collide with captions, progress
+indicators, the table of contents or the navigation controls. Prefer the project-local
+`scripts/inspect-presentation.mjs`; if it is unavailable, write any temporary Playwright helper under
+the project root so dependencies resolve locally, never in a path outside the project.
+
+Review every `WARN` the helper prints, step by step: fix accidental text or chrome collisions, give the
+active progress/TOC entry a visibly distinct style, and style the attribution link so it is legible. Mark
+only genuinely intentional, readable overlaps with `allowOverlap`, then rerun the helper. The warnings
+are advisory, so report any that remain, with the reason.
+
+Quality bar for every presentation: builds with no type errors; renders the first step with no runtime
+or console errors; shows a caption per step; supports next/previous; passes the visual check; follows the
+evolving-scene model.
+
+## 5. Report
+
+State the route (`/<slug>`), the files changed, the build and verify results, and any remaining advisory
+warnings. Keep unrelated files and other presentations exactly as they were.
diff --git a/skills/presentation/scripts/presentation-scaffold.mjs b/skills/presentation/scripts/presentation-scaffold.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..895646a355dd800decb366f69f23387f9ff9c5b6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/skills/presentation/scripts/presentation-scaffold.mjs
@@ -0,0 +1,361 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env node
+// Deterministic helpers behind the presentation skill: detect the scaffold
+// anchors, resolve the target, scaffold what is missing, and add presentations.
+//   node presentation-scaffold.mjs detect <dir>
+//   node presentation-scaffold.mjs scaffold <dir> [--yes] [--no-install] [--no-browser]
+//   node presentation-scaffold.mjs add <target> --slug <slug> --title <title>
+// Templates are resolved relative to this skill's own directory (the one that holds SKILL.md).
+import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'
+import {
+  copyFileSync,
+  existsSync,
+  mkdirSync,
+  readFileSync,
+  readdirSync,
+  writeFileSync,
+} from 'node:fs'
+import path from 'node:path'
+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'
+
+export const SKILL_DIR = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..')
+export const BOOTSTRAP_DIR = path.join(SKILL_DIR, 'templates/bootstrap')
+export const PRESENTATION_DIR = path.join(SKILL_DIR, 'templates/presentation')
+
+/** Which bootstrap files make up each anchor. */
+const KIT_PREFIX = 'src/presentation-kit/'
+const INDEX_FILES = new Set([
+  'src/presentations/index.ts',
+  'src/main.tsx',
+  'src/router.tsx',
+  'src/routes.ts',
+  'src/Landing.tsx',
+  'src/index.css',
+])
+
+export function anchorOf(relativeFile) {
+  if (relativeFile.startsWith(KIT_PREFIX)) return 'kit'
+  if (INDEX_FILES.has(relativeFile)) return 'index'
+  return 'build'
+}
+
+const readJson = (file) => JSON.parse(readFileSync(file, 'utf8'))
+
+function listFiles(dir) {
+  return readdirSync(dir, { recursive: true, withFileTypes: true })
+    .filter((entry) => entry.isFile())
+    .map((entry) => path.relative(dir, path.join(entry.parentPath, entry.name)).split(path.sep).join('/'))
+    .sort()
+}
+
+function allDeps(pkg) {
+  return { ...pkg?.dependencies, ...pkg?.devDependencies }
+}
+
+/** Contract-level anchor detection for one app directory. */
+export function detectAnchors(dir) {
+  const pkgFile = path.join(dir, 'package.json')
+  let build = false
+  if (existsSync(pkgFile)) {
+    try {
+      const pkg = readJson(pkgFile)
+      const deps = allDeps(pkg)
+      build = Boolean(pkg.scripts?.build) && ['vite', 'react', 'typescript'].every((d) => d in deps)
+    } catch {
+      build = false
+    }
+  }
+  // Kit and index count only when they export something: an empty or comment-only file is no contract.
+  const exportsSomething = (file) => existsSync(file) && /^\s*export\s/m.test(readFileSync(file, 'utf8'))
+  const find = (folder, pattern) =>
+    existsSync(folder) ? readdirSync(folder).filter((name) => pattern.test(name)).map((name) => path.join(folder, name)) : []
+  const kitDir = path.join(dir, 'src/presentation-kit')
+  const kit =
+    find(kitDir, /^Presentation\.[jt]sx?$/).some(exportsSomething) &&
+    find(kitDir, /^types\.[jt]s$/).some(exportsSomething)
+  const index = find(path.join(dir, 'src/presentations'), /^index\.tsx?$/).some(exportsSomething)
+  return { build, kit, index }
+}
+
+export function isMonorepo(dir) {
+  const pkgFile = path.join(dir, 'package.json')
+  if (existsSync(pkgFile)) {
+    try {
+      if (readJson(pkgFile).workspaces) return true
+    } catch {
+      /* unreadable manifest: fall through to the other signals */
+    }
+  }
+  return ['pnpm-workspace.yaml', 'packages', 'apps'].some((name) => existsSync(path.join(dir, name)))
+}
+
+function isProjectEmpty(dir) {
+  return !existsSync(dir) || readdirSync(dir).filter((n) => n !== '.git').length === 0
+}
+
+/**
+ * Where the presentation app belongs and what it is missing.
+ * - Already inside a presentation app (scene kit or index at the root) -> use it.
+ * - Monorepo -> a self-contained app in `presentations/`.
+ * - Otherwise the project root.
+ */
+export function detect(dir) {
+  const root = path.resolve(dir)
+  const rootAnchors = detectAnchors(root)
+  const monorepo = isMonorepo(root)
+  const nested = path.join(root, 'presentations')
+  const nestedApp = existsSync(nested) && Object.values(detectAnchors(nested)).some(Boolean)
+  const insideApp = rootAnchors.kit || rootAnchors.index
+  const target = !insideApp && (nestedApp || monorepo) ? nested : root
+  const anchors = target === root ? rootAnchors : detectAnchors(nested)
+  const missing = Object.keys(anchors).filter((name) => !anchors[name])
+  const projectEmpty = isProjectEmpty(root)
+  return {
+    root,
+    target,
+    monorepo,
+    projectEmpty,
+    anchors,
+    missing,
+    // A non-empty project that lacks the kit or the index is confirmed with the user before writing.
+    needsConfirmation: !projectEmpty && (missing.includes('kit') || missing.includes('index')),
+  }
+}
+
+/** Adds missing dependencies and scripts without touching what the project already has. */
+export function mergePackageJson(existing, template) {
+  const merged = { ...existing }
+  const added = []
+  for (const field of ['dependencies', 'devDependencies']) {
+    const have = allDeps(existing)
+    for (const [name, version] of Object.entries(template[field] ?? {})) {
+      if (name in have) continue
+      merged[field] = { ...merged[field], [name]: version }
+      added.push(name)
+    }
+  }
+  for (const [name, command] of Object.entries(template.scripts ?? {})) {
+    if (existing.scripts?.[name]) continue
+    merged.scripts = { ...merged.scripts, [name]: command }
+  }
+  return { merged, added }
+}
+
+const ROUTED_ENTRY = `import { presentations } from './presentations'
+import { resolveRoute } from './routes'
+
+// Presentation routes get the router; every other path keeps the host app's original entry.
+if (resolveRoute(window.location.pathname, presentations)) {
+  void Promise.all([import('react'), import('react-dom/client'), import('./router')]).then(
+    ([{ StrictMode }, { createRoot }, { Router }]) => {
+      createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(
+        <StrictMode>
+          <Router pathname={window.location.pathname} registry={presentations} />
+        </StrictMode>,
+      )
+    },
+  )
+} else {
+  void import('./app-main')
+}
+`
+
+/**
+ * An existing app entry keeps mounting the host app, so presentation routes would never render.
+ * Move it to `app-main.tsx` and put a routed entry in its place. Returns whether it rewired.
+ */
+function wireEntry(target, existing) {
+  const moved = path.join(target, 'src/app-main.tsx')
+  if (/presentations/.test(existing) || existsSync(moved)) return false
+  writeFileSync(moved, existing)
+  writeFileSync(path.join(target, 'src/main.tsx'), ROUTED_ENTRY)
+  return true
+}
+
+const escapeRegex = (text) => text.replace(/[.+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, '\\$&')
+
+/** Whether a workspace glob (`dir`, `dir/*`, `dir/**`, `apps/*\/web`) matches a root-relative path. */
+function workspaceGlobMatches(glob, rel) {
+  const clean = glob.replace(/^\.\//, '').replace(/\/+$/, '')
+  const source = clean
+    .split('**')
+    .map((part) => part.split('*').map(escapeRegex).join('[^/]+'))
+    .join('.*')
+  return new RegExp(`^${source}$`).test(rel)
+}
+
+/** Whether a parent package.json lists `target` among its npm workspaces (honouring `!` exclusions). */
+export function isWorkspaceMember(target) {
+  const dir = path.resolve(target)
+  for (let parent = path.dirname(dir); ; parent = path.dirname(parent)) {
+    const pkgFile = path.join(parent, 'package.json')
+    if (existsSync(pkgFile)) {
+      try {
+        const { workspaces } = readJson(pkgFile)
+        const listed = (Array.isArray(workspaces) ? workspaces : (workspaces?.packages ?? [])).filter(
+          (pattern) => typeof pattern === 'string',
+        )
+        const rel = path.relative(parent, dir).split(path.sep).join('/')
+        const included = listed.filter((p) => !p.startsWith('!')).some((p) => workspaceGlobMatches(p, rel))
+        const excluded = listed.filter((p) => p.startsWith('!')).some((p) => workspaceGlobMatches(p.slice(1), rel))
+        if (included && !excluded) return true
+      } catch {
+        /* unreadable manifest: not a workspace root */
+      }
+    }
+    if (parent === path.dirname(parent)) return false
+  }
+}
+
+/**
+ * `npm ci` needs the lockfile of the npm project root. A workspace member's own lockfile does not
+ * count (npm demands the root's), so members, and manifests that gained dependencies, use `npm install`.
+ */
+export function installCommand(target, addedDeps = []) {
+  const ownLock = existsSync(path.join(target, 'package-lock.json'))
+  return ownLock && addedDeps.length === 0 && !isWorkspaceMember(target) ? 'ci' : 'install'
+}
+
+/** Writes the files of the missing anchors; existing files are never overwritten. */
+export function scaffold(dir, { install = true, browser = true } = {}) {
+  const info = detect(dir)
+  const { target } = info
+  mkdirSync(target, { recursive: true })
+  const written = []
+  const entryFile = path.join(target, 'src/main.tsx')
+  const existingEntry = existsSync(entryFile) ? readFileSync(entryFile, 'utf8') : null
+  const templatePkg = readJson(path.join(BOOTSTRAP_DIR, 'package.json'))
+
+  for (const file of listFiles(BOOTSTRAP_DIR)) {
+    // The verification scripts back the npm commands added below, so they are ensured on every run.
+    if (!file.startsWith('scripts/') && !info.missing.includes(anchorOf(file))) continue
+    const dest = path.join(target, file)
+    if (existsSync(dest)) continue
+    if (file === 'package-lock.json' && existsSync(path.join(target, 'package.json'))) continue
+    mkdirSync(path.dirname(dest), { recursive: true })
+    copyFileSync(path.join(BOOTSTRAP_DIR, file), dest)
+    written.push(file)
+  }
+
+  const entryWired = info.missing.includes('index') && existingEntry !== null && wireEntry(target, existingEntry)
+
+  // The dependency set is never assumed: add whatever the manifest lacks.
+  let addedDeps = []
+  const pkgFile = path.join(target, 'package.json')
+  if (existsSync(pkgFile)) {
+    const { merged, added } = mergePackageJson(readJson(pkgFile), templatePkg)
+    if (added.length > 0 || JSON.stringify(merged) !== JSON.stringify(readJson(pkgFile))) {
+      writeFileSync(pkgFile, JSON.stringify(merged, null, 2) + '\n')
+    }
+    addedDeps = added
+  }
+
+  let installed = false
+  const needsInstall = written.includes('package.json') || addedDeps.length > 0 || !existsSync(path.join(target, 'node_modules'))
+  if (install && needsInstall) {
+    let command = installCommand(target, addedDeps)
+    let result = spawnSync('npm', [command], { cwd: target, stdio: 'inherit' })
+    if (result.status !== 0 && command === 'ci') {
+      // `npm ci` is only a reproducibility preference; a lockfile it cannot use (for example a workspace
+      // layout the detection above missed) must not stop the scaffold.
+      console.error(`warning: npm ci failed in ${target}; retrying with npm install.`)
+      command = 'install'
+      result = spawnSync('npm', [command], { cwd: target, stdio: 'inherit' })
+    }
+    if (result.status !== 0) throw new Error(`npm ${command} failed in ${target}`)
+    installed = true
+  }
+  // Render verification needs a Chromium build; a fresh checkout has none cached.
+  let browserInstalled = false
+  if (install && browser) {
+    const result = spawnSync('npx', ['playwright', 'install', 'chromium'], { cwd: target, stdio: 'inherit' })
+    browserInstalled = result.status === 0 && !result.error
+    if (!browserInstalled) {
+      console.error(
+        `warning: could not install Chromium (${result.error?.message ?? `exit ${result.status}`}). Run "npx playwright install chromium" in ${target} before npm run verify.`,
+      )
+    }
+  }
+  return { ...info, written, addedDeps, installed, browserInstalled, entryWired }
+}
+
+/** CSS-class / id prefix derived from a slug. */
+export function nameFromSlug(slug) {
+  return slug.replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/gi, '-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '').toLowerCase()
+}
+
+/** Placeholders: `__TITLE_JSON__` is a JS string literal, `__TITLE__` is comment-safe plain text. */
+function fill(text, values) {
+  const replacements = {
+    SLUG: values.slug,
+    TITLE_JSON: JSON.stringify(values.title),
+    TITLE: values.title.replaceAll('*/', '* /'),
+    NAME: values.name,
+  }
+  // One pass with a function replacer: user text is never re-scanned or read as `$` patterns.
+  return text.replace(/__(SLUG|TITLE_JSON|TITLE|NAME)__/g, (_match, key) => replacements[key])
+}
+
+/** Creates `src/presentations/<slug>/` from the template and registers it. */
+export function addPresentation(target, { slug, title }) {
+  if (!/^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$/.test(slug)) throw new Error(`invalid slug "${slug}": use lowercase words joined by "-"`)
+  const registryFile = ['index.ts', 'index.tsx']
+    .map((name) => path.join(target, 'src/presentations', name))
+    .find((file) => existsSync(file)) ?? path.join(target, 'src/presentations/index.ts')
+  if (!existsSync(registryFile)) throw new Error(`no presentation index at ${registryFile}; scaffold first`)
+  const folder = path.join(target, 'src/presentations', slug)
+  if (existsSync(folder)) throw new Error(`presentation "${slug}" already exists`)
+  const registry = readFileSync(registryFile, 'utf8')
+  if (new RegExp(`slug:\\s*['"]${slug}['"]`).test(registry)) throw new Error(`slug "${slug}" is already registered`)
+
+  const values = { slug, title, name: nameFromSlug(slug) }
+  for (const file of listFiles(PRESENTATION_DIR)) {
+    const dest = path.join(folder, file)
+    mkdirSync(path.dirname(dest), { recursive: true })
+    writeFileSync(dest, fill(readFileSync(path.join(PRESENTATION_DIR, file), 'utf8'), values))
+  }
+
+  const close = registry.lastIndexOf(']')
+  const entry = `  {\n    slug: ${JSON.stringify(slug)},\n    title: ${JSON.stringify(title)},\n    load: () => import('./${slug}/Talk'),\n  },\n`
+  writeFileSync(registryFile, registry.slice(0, close) + entry + registry.slice(close))
+  return { folder, registryFile }
+}
+
+function main(argv) {
+  const [command, dir, ...rest] = argv
+  const option = (name) => {
+    const at = rest.indexOf(name)
+    return at === -1 ? undefined : rest[at + 1]
+  }
+  if (command === 'detect' && dir) {
+    console.log(JSON.stringify(detect(dir), null, 2))
+  } else if (command === 'scaffold' && dir) {
+    const info = detect(dir)
+    if (info.missing.length === 0) {
+      console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...info, written: [], skipped: 'all anchors present' }, null, 2))
+    } else if (info.needsConfirmation && !rest.includes('--yes')) {
+      console.error(
+        `CONFIRM: the project is not empty. Scaffolding ${info.missing.join(', ')} into ${info.target}. Ask the user, then rerun with --yes.`,
+      )
+      process.exit(2)
+    } else {
+      console.log(JSON.stringify(scaffold(dir, { install: !rest.includes('--no-install'), browser: !rest.includes('--no-browser') }), null, 2))
+    }
+  } else if (command === 'add' && dir) {
+    const slug = option('--slug')
+    const title = option('--title')
+    if (!slug || !title) throw new Error('add needs --slug and --title')
+    console.log(JSON.stringify(addPresentation(path.resolve(dir), { slug, title }), null, 2))
+  } else {
+    console.error('usage: presentation-scaffold.mjs detect|scaffold|add <dir> [options]')
+    process.exit(64)
+  }
+}
+
+if (process.argv[1] && path.resolve(process.argv[1]) === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) {
+  try {
+    main(process.argv.slice(2))
+  } catch (error) {
+    console.error(`error: ${error.message}`)
+    process.exit(1)
+  }
+}
